# Built installers, served locally by the dev server. Binaries do not belong in git.
# public/downloads/  (see below)

# Edge function secrets. Anthropic and Stripe keys live here.
supabase/.env.functions
.vercel

# Apple signing credentials. Never commit.
.env.signing

# Rust build output. 5.7GB of incremental artifacts, regenerated by cargo.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# Product footage.
#
# Not ignored. It is shot against Sidq's own backdrop window rather than off
# somebody's desktop, so there is nothing personal in the frame, and the site
# cannot serve what a build off GitHub never receives.

# The signed, notarised installers the download button points at.
#
# Vercel builds this site from GitHub, so anything gitignored is simply absent
# from the deploy — which is how the download button ended up pointing at files
# that were not there. 19MB of binary in a repository is not lovely, and it is
# better than a 404 on the only button that matters.
!public/downloads/
!public/downloads/*.dmg

# The packaged extension upload. Rebuilt by scripts/package-extension.sh.
dist-extension/
